# Monorepo root.
#
# Both apps are tracked here now: web-app/galactic-weather and
# ios-app/galacticweather. Each keeps its own .gitignore for app-specific rules
# (node_modules and .next for web; generated .xcodeproj and Config/Secrets.xcconfig
# for iOS), and those still apply within their subtrees.
#
# This file covers only what belongs to the root.

# Superseded .git directories from the pre-monorepo layout, kept rather than
# deleted. The web repo's history became this repo's history; the iOS repo's was
# subtree-merged in and also still lives at robleto/galactic-weather-ios.
/.git-rootrepo-superseded/
/.git-iosrepo-superseded/

# Prior incarnations of the project. Large, and not part of the build.
/archive/

# Build output and editor state. Deliberately NOT root-anchored — VSCode drops a
# .history/ beside each workspace it opens, so web-app/.history/ exists too and
# an anchored pattern silently misses it (953 files, in this case).
.history/
.next/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# NOT ignoring .claude/ — web-app/galactic-weather/.claude/launch.json is a
# tracked dev-server config that preview tooling reads, and an ignore rule here
# would silently drop it in this restructure.

# Xcode. The project file is generated from project.yml by XcodeGen and must not
# be committed — see the Testing section of CLAUDE.md.
*.xcodeproj
DerivedData/
xcuserdata/
.swiftpm/

# Release archives from scripts/archive.sh. Root-anchored because this is the one
# build directory the script owns. An .xcarchive runs to hundreds of MB and a new
# one lands on every run — the script never deletes old ones, per the deletion
# policy in CLAUDE.md, so without this rule they accumulate straight into commits.
/build/
